## Why This Is Asked
This question tests practical use of SageMaker multi-model endpoints, per-tenant routing, and controlled releases under data privacy constraints (PrivateLink). It blends model choice, infrastructure sizing, and a measurable validation plan suitable for entry-level engineers.

## Key Concepts
- SageMaker multi-model endpoints and Model Registry
- Tenant-aware routing with API Gateway + Lambda
- PrivateLink data isolation and VPC considerations
- Canary rollouts and rollback criteria

## Code Example
```javascript
// Pseudocode for tenant routing to a variant
function routeTenant(req){
  const tenant = req.headers['x-tenant'];
  const variant = registry.getVariant(tenant);
  return endpoint.invoke({Body: req.body, Variant: variant});
}
```

## Follow-up Questions
- How would you test tenant isolation in practice?
- How would you monitor per-tenant drift and trigger rollbacks?

## Why This Is Asked

This question probes designing a latency-sensitive, privacy-respecting, explainable inference service with multi-tenant isolation in AWS, plus lifecycle and cost awareness.

## Key Concepts

- PrivateLink, VPC, Private Data Lake, per-tenant isolation
- SageMaker endpoints, Feature Store, Model Registry
- Real-time explainability paths (Clarify/SHAP) with low latency
- Canary rollout, drift detection, monitoring and cost

## Code Example

```javascript
// Example: route to appropriate prod/canary endpoint
function route(tenantId){
  const inCanary = ['tenantA','tenantB'];
  const ep = inCanary.includes(tenantId) ? 'fraud-prod-canary' : 'fraud-prod';
  return ep;
}
```

## Follow-up Questions

- How would you enforce strict per-tenant data access controls across services?
- How would you validate explainability fidelity at high throughput?
- How would you handle retraining triggers when drift is detected per tenant?
